* =============================================================================
* Differential device library (ngspice)
* Sources for every model are listed in docs/research/sources_technical.yaml and
* summarised in docs/hand_calcs.md. Model cards are used unmodified unless a
* comment says otherwise.
* =============================================================================

* --- Small-signal NPN, 2N3904 ------------------------------------------------
* onsemi MODPEX model (Aug 2001), parameters verbatim from the onsemi model
* library distributed "with permission of ON Semiconductor" (source key
* onsemi_spice_models_volta); renamed Q2N3904 for readability.
.model Q2N3904 NPN(IS=1.26532e-10 BF=206.302 NF=1.5 VAF=1000
+ IKF=0.0272221 ISE=2.30771e-09 NE=3.31052 BR=20.6302
+ NR=2.89609 VAR=9.39809 IKR=0.272221 ISC=2.30771e-09
+ NC=1.9876 RB=5.8376 IRB=50.3624 RBM=0.634251
+ RE=0.0001 RC=2.65711 XTB=0.1 XTI=1
+ EG=1.05 CJE=4.64214e-12 VJE=0.4 MJE=0.256227
+ TF=4.19578e-10 XTF=0.906167 VTF=8.75418 ITF=0.0105823
+ CJC=3.76961e-12 VJC=0.4 MJC=0.238109 XCJC=0.8
+ FC=0.512134 CJS=0 VJS=0.75 MJS=0.5
+ TR=6.82023e-08 PTF=0 KF=0 AF=1)

* --- Small-signal switching diode, 1N4148 ---------------------------------------
* Diodes Inc. model DI_1N4148, parameters verbatim (source key diodes_inc_switching_diode_spice).
.model D1N4148 D(IS=222p RS=68.6m BV=75.0 IBV=1.00u CJO=4.00p M=0.333 N=1.65 TT=5.76n)

* --- 16 V zener, 1N4745A ----------------------------------------------------------
* Diodes Inc. subcircuit DI_1N4745A (source key diodes_inc_zener_spice): forward
* diode DF, reverse path DR in series with VZ = 14.6 V. Only change: VZ is read
* from parameter node PVZ (nominal 14.6 V) so Monte Carlo draws can apply the
* +-5 % zener-voltage tolerance with 'alter'. Terminals: A (anode), K (cathode).
.subckt ZENER_1N4745A A K PVZ
D1 A K DF_1N4745A
DZ n3 A DR_1N4745A
BVZ K n3 V = V(PVZ)
.model DF_1N4745A D(IS=25.7p RS=0.620 N=1.10 CJO=74.4p VJ=1.00 M=0.330 TT=50.1n)
.model DR_1N4745A D(IS=5.15f RS=0.897 N=1.80)
.ends ZENER_1N4745A

* =============================================================================
* Triode (12AX7 / ECC83 class): N. Koren's 12AX7 "NEW MODEL" (Glass Audio, 1996;
* library listing, source key koren_tube_lib_1996_mirror). Plate current:
*   E1 = (Vpk/KP) * ln(1 + exp(KP*(1/MU + Vgk/sqrt(KVB + Vpk^2))))
*   Ip = (E1^EX + sgn(E1)*|E1|^EX) / KG1        (= 2*E1^EX/KG1 for E1 > 0)
* Published 12AX7 parameters: MU=100 EX=1.4 KG1=1060 KP=600 KVB=300 RGI=2000,
* CCG=2.3p CGP=2.4p CCP=0.9p.
* Project changes (behaviour-preserving):
*   - ln(1+exp(x)) is evaluated as uramp(x) + ln(1+exp(-abs(x))): identical value,
*     no overflow, continuous derivative (smooth for Newton iteration).
*   - MU and KG1 come from parameter nodes PMU and PKG (volts) so Monte Carlo draws
*     can vary them with 'alter'. PV scales emission: 1 = nominal, 0.3-0.6 = worn
*     cathode (low emission), 0 = heater open (no conduction).
*   - |E1|^EX + sgn(E1)|E1|^EX is written as 2*max(E1,0)^EX (identical value;
*     ngspice B sources have no signed-power function).
*   - Grid current: Koren's diode DX in series with RGI = 2k, verbatim.
* =============================================================================
.subckt TRIODE_KOREN P G K PV PMU PKG
Bx x 0 V = 600*(1/V(PMU) + V(G,K)/sqrt(300 + V(P,K)*V(P,K)))
Be1 e1 0 V = (V(P,K)/600)*(uramp(V(x)) + ln(1 + exp(-abs(V(x)))))
Bp P K I = V(PV)*2*pwr(uramp(V(e1)),1.4)/V(PKG)
D3 gg K DX_KOREN
RGI G gg 2000
.model DX_KOREN D(IS=1N RS=1 CJO=10PF TT=1N)
Rpk P K 1G
Cgk G K 2.3p
Cgp G P 2.4p
Cpk P K 0.9p
.ends TRIODE_KOREN

* =============================================================================
* Behavioural op-amp (FET-input, TL07x class): single-pole, finite gain-bandwidth,
* output swing limited to 1.5 V inside each rail by a smooth tanh limiter.
*   A0 = 2e5 (106 dB); GBW (MHz) read from parameter node PGBW; dominant pole
*   = GBW/A0. PDEAD = 1 forces the output to a rail (PRAIL = 1 -> top rail,
*   0 -> bottom rail); PDEAD = 0 is normal operation.
* =============================================================================
.subckt OPAMP_BEH INP INM OUT VCC VEE PGBW PDEAD PRAIL
Rin INP INM 10Meg
Bmid mid 0 V = 0.5*(V(VCC) + V(VEE))
* gm = 2*pi*GBW*C1 with C1 = 1 nF and GBW in MHz -> 6.2832e-3 * V(PGBW) S
Bgm mid n1 I = 6.2832e-3*V(PGBW)*V(INP,INM)
R1 n1 mid {2e5/(6.2832e-3*3)}
C1 n1 mid 1n
Bout outi 0 V = (1 - V(PDEAD))*(V(mid) + (0.5*(V(VCC) - V(VEE)) - 1.5)*tanh((V(n1) - V(mid))/(0.5*(V(VCC) - V(VEE)) - 1.5)))
+ + V(PDEAD)*(V(PRAIL)*(V(VCC) - 1.5) + (1 - V(PRAIL))*(V(VEE) + 1.5))
Rout outi OUT 50
Iq VCC VEE DC 2.5m
.ends OPAMP_BEH
